{"family": "pointdit", "task": "depth", "name": "PointDiT", "plain": "Google's PointDiT: a diffusion transformer that denoises a 3D point map in three steps from one image, conditioned on frozen DINOv3 features. Code and weights are Apache-2.0; the DINOv3 encoder it loads is under the DINOv3 License.", "summary": "PointDiT (Xu et al., Google 2026): monocular geometry as generation; a pixel-space diffusion transformer denoises a point map in 3 Euler steps, conditioned on frozen DINOv3 features of the image. Outputs an affine-invariant point map and its depth.", "tier": "experimental", "upstream": "https://github.com/google-research/pointdit", "upstream_commit": "11f53a30aeb4d34d49d2beda655ee6f19b2ad7f8", "original_is": null, "papers": [{"title": "PointDiT: Pixel-Space Diffusion for Monocular Geometry Estimation", "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.02515", "date": "2026-07-02", "venue": "ICML 2026", "variants": []}], "official": [], "modes": ["portable", "kernels"], "portable_dtype": "float16", "kernels_dtype": "float16", "kernel_libs": ["fastbb", "dpt_fused"], "mps_kernel_libs": [], "mps_dtypes": ["float32", "float16"], "no_kernels_reason": "", "no_original_reason": "", "options": [{"name": "tokens", "default": 1024, "bounds": ">= 1", "effect": "output"}, {"name": "steps", "default": 3, "bounds": ">= 1", "effect": "output"}], "outputs": [{"name": "points", "extra": false}, {"name": "depth", "extra": false}], "output_info": {"kind": "affine_invariant"}, "licence_files": ["LICENSE"], "licence_notes": ["The PointDiT code and weights are Apache-2.0; the frozen DINOv3 ViT-B/16 and ViT-L/16 encoders are under the DINOv3 License (Meta: attribution and conditions apply; gated on Hugging Face); read it before commercial use."], "limitations": ["Affine-invariant output: points up to an unknown scale and 3-D shift, depth (their z) up to scale and shift; align before use.", "Trained at 512 x 512: inputs are resized to about `tokens` 16-pixel patches at their aspect ratio (bilinear) and the point map is resized back with nearest, as the original's wild-image path.", "Kernels mode captures CUDA graphs: the graph's private memory pool and static outputs stay reserved after the call, so peak reserved is above portable by ~85 MiB (b), more for l (peak allocated is equal or lower); `cuda_graphs=false` or `release_graphs()` frees it at the cost of launch overhead."], "task_io": "Input: one RGB image. Output: a depth or inverse-depth map. `kind` (a card field, `result.kind`) says what the numbers mean: `metric` = metres; `scale_invariant`, `affine_invariant`, `affine_invariant_log` (log depth) and `affine_invariant_inverse` are relative (unknown scale or shift, not metres). Metric models that use the focal length take `model(image, intrinsics=K)` (K `[3, 3]`, pixels of the input): `metric3d-vit-large` and `da3metric-large` need it for correct metres (`da3metric-large`: metres = output x focal / 300; without `intrinsics=` a 300 px focal length is assumed, wrong for a real camera). `unidepth-v2-vitl14`, `unik3d-vitl`, `depth-pro` and MoGe estimate the camera themselves (given `intrinsics=` replace `fx`); `zoedepth-nk` and the relative models (`da3mono-large` too) take none. Normals-only models (`kind` `none`) return `result.normals` `[B, H, W, 3]` (unit vectors, camera frame: x right, y down, z forward).", "install": {"extras": [], "noncommercial_weights": []}, "variants": [{"id": "pointdit-b-512", "released": "0.2.0", "added_in": "0.2.0", "ref": "pointdit-b-512@1", "name": "pointdit-b-512", "setting": "", "default_tag": false, "params": {"arch": "b", "encoder": "dinov3-vitb16"}, "licence": {"code": "Apache-2.0", "code_class": "permissive", "weights": "LicenseRef-DINOv3-License", "weights_assumed": false, "evidence": "https://github.com/google-research/pointdit/blob/11f53a30aeb4d34d49d2beda655ee6f19b2ad7f8/LICENSE (Apache-2.0); https://huggingface.co/haofeixu/pointdit (license: apache-2.0); encoder: https://huggingface.co/facebook/dinov3-vitl16-pretrain-lvd1689m (DINOv3 License, gated)", "training_data": [{"id": "unstated", "name": "not stated by the authors"}], "training_note": "Mixture of synthetic and real point-map datasets (\"mixdata\") per the PointDiT paper; the DINOv3 encoder: LVD-1689M (not released)", "commercial": "yes", "reasons": [], "notes": ["data: unstated"]}, "weights": [{"name": "dinov3-vitb16-pretrain-lvd1689m/model.safetensors", "sha256": "9a21ac3df0c63839d62612dda6f454d816c25611cc7a52966ed5a5a94921dc8b", "size": 342662192, "url": "https://huggingface.co/facebook/dinov3-vitb16-pretrain-lvd1689m/resolve/5931719e67bbdb9737e363e781fb0c67687896bc/model.safetensors", "host": "Hugging Face", "member": null, "archive_size": null, "mirror": null}, {"name": "pointditb-512-mixdata-nodinov3-1d42aacf.pth", "sha256": "1d42aacfd6aaf97c8bd96b0ce5e23bd880cd01b2efbb2ac80ccf8876fde3034b", "size": 1097860526, "url": "https://huggingface.co/haofeixu/pointdit/resolve/956a6f4279c20b59adfc1ea2038603514f4fe5dc/pointditb-512-mixdata-nodinov3-1d42aacf.pth", "host": "Hugging Face", "member": null, "archive_size": null, "mirror": null}], "input_size": "any H x W >= 1, resized or padded inside the model", "tested_max": {"size": "3000x4000", "alloc_mib": 843, "reserved_mib": 1074}, "speed": {"standard": "994x1482", "inputs": [{"input": "518x770", "scene": "synthetic", "standard": false, "modes": {"portable": {"ms": 30.732, "ms_min": 30.604, "noise": 0.0036, "runs": 15, "peak_alloc_mb": 432, "peak_reserved_mb": 504, "load_s": 1.67, "first_call_s": 0.184, "import_s": 0.04, "scene": "synthetic", "date": "2026-11-16", "torch": "2.14.1+cu130", "protocol": "first call, 3 warm-up, peak reset, median of 3 rounds x median of 5", "dtype": "float16", "commit": "33b2432c+dir"}, "kernels": {"ms": 20.807, "ms_min": 20.593, "noise": 0.0011, "runs": 15, "peak_alloc_mb": 434, "peak_reserved_mb": 570, "load_s": 1.74, "first_call_s": 0.155, "import_s": 0.04, "scene": "synthetic", "date": "2026-11-16", "torch": "2.14.1+cu130", "protocol": 